<title>GERMANY: Buderus mulls sale of unit to UK's BSG.</title>
<headline>Buderus mulls sale of unit to UK's BSG.</headline>
<dateline>WETZLAR, Germany 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>German engineering group Buderus AG said on Wednesday it was in talks with BSG International on the possible sale of its Buderus Sell GmbH and other units to the British aircraft outfitters.</p>
<p>Buderus said that BSG International and Buderus Sell were among the world's leading aircraft outfitters and said a merger of the two companies would allow the them to expand their already good market positions globally.</p>
<p>Together with its subsidiaries, Buderus Sell had 442 employees and turnover of 106 million marks in the year to the end of September 1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
